>`.\n1707 | \n1708 |     Returns\n1709 |     -------\n1710 |     X : array of shape `shape`\n1711 |         The generated array.\n1712 | \n1713 |     rows : array of shape (n_clusters, X.shape[0],)\n1714 |         The indicators for cluster membership of each row.\n1715 | \n1716 |     cols : array of shape (n_clusters, X.shape[1],)\n1717 |         The indicators for cluster membership of each column.\n1718 | \n1719 | \n1720 |     References\n1721 |     ----------\n1722 | \n1723 |     .. [1] Kluger, Y., Basri, R., Chang, J. T., & Gerstein, M. (2003).\n1724 |         Spectral biclustering of microarray data: coclustering genes\n1725 |         and conditions. Genome research, 13(4), 703-716.\n1726 | \n1727 |     See also\n1728 |     --------\n1729 |     make_biclusters\n1730 |     \"\"\"\n1731 |     generator = check_random_state(random_state)\n1732 | \n1733 |     if hasattr(n_clusters, \"__len__\"):\n1734 |         n_row_clusters, n_col_clusters = n_clusters\n1735 |     else:\n1736 |         n_row_clusters = n_col_clusters = n_clusters\n1737 | \n1738 |     # row and column clusters of approximately equal sizes\n1739 |     n_rows, n_cols = shape\n1740 |     row_sizes = generator.multinomial(n_rows,\n1741 |                                       np.repeat(1.0 / n_row_clusters,\n1742 |                                                 n_row_clusters))\n1743 |     col_sizes = generator.multinomial(n_cols,\n1744 |                                       np.repeat(1.0 / n_col_clusters,\n1745 |                                                 n_col_clusters))\n1746 | \n1747 |     row_labels = np.hstack(list(np.repeat(val, rep) for val, rep in\n1748 |                                 zip(range(n_row_clusters), row_sizes)))\n1749 |     col_labels = np.hstack(list(np.repeat(val, rep) for val, rep in\n1750 |                                 zip(range(n_col_clusters), col_sizes)))\n1751 | \n1752 |     result = np.zeros(shape, dtype=np.float64)\n1753 |     for i in range(n_row_clusters):\n1754 |         for j in range(n_col_clusters):\n1755 |             selector = np.outer(row_labels == i, col_labels == j)\n1756 |             result[selector] += generator.uniform(minval, maxval)\n1757 | \n1758 |     if noise > 0:\n1759 |         result += generator.normal(scale=noise, size=result.shape)\n1760 | \n1761 |     if shuffle:\n1762 |         result, row_idx, col_idx = _shuffle(result, random_state)\n1763 |         row_labels = row_labels[row_idx]\n1764 |         col_labels = col_labels[col_idx]\n1765 | \n1766 |     rows = np.vstack([row_labels == label\n1767 |                       for label in range(n_row_clusters)\n1768 |                       for _ in range(n_col_clusters)])\n1769 |     cols = np.vstack([col_labels == label\n1770 |                       for _ in range(n_row_clusters)\n1771 |                       for label in range(n_col_clusters)])\n1772 | \n1773 |     return result, rows, cols\n```\n"}, {"content": "Let me search for the specific implementation of the checksum validation functionality.\n\n<function=search_code_snippets>\n<parameter=search_terms>['_stream_checksum_generator']</parameter>\n", "role": "assistant", "tool_calls": null, "function_call": null}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "toolu_01", "name": "search_code_snippets", "content": "OBSERVATION:\nsklearn/utils/validation.py:_check_fit_params\nsklearn/datasets/_rcv1.py:fetch_rcv1\nsklearn/datasets/_rcv1.py:fetch_rcv1\nsklearn/datasets/_openml.py:fetch_openml\nsklearn/datasets/_samples_generator.py:make_classification\nsklearn/datasets/_rcv1.py:fetch_rcv1\nsklearn/datasets/_samples_generator.py:make_classification\n##Searching for term \"_stream_checksum_generator\"...\n### Search Result:\nFound code snippet in file `sklearn/datasets/_rcv1.py`.\nSource: Retrieved code content using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n  1 | \"\"\"RCV1 dataset.\n  2 | \n  3 | The dataset page is available at\n  4 | \n  5 |     http://jmlr.csail.mit.edu/papers/volume5/lewis04a/\n  6 | \"\"\"\n  7 | \n  