validate again for each call to partial_fit\n1350 |             partial_fit_and_fitted = (\n1351 |                 fit_method.__name__ == \"partial_fit\" and _is_fitted(estimator)\n1352 |             )\n1353 | \n1354 |             if not global_skip_validation and not partial_fit_and_fitted:\n1355 |                 estimator._validate_params()\n1356 | \n1357 |             with config_context(\n1358 |                 skip_parameter_validation=(\n1359 |                     prefer_skip_nested_validation or global_skip_validation\n1360 |                 )\n1361 |             ):\n1362 |                 return fit_method(estimator, *args, **kwargs)\n1363 | \n1364 |         return wrapper\n1365 | \n1366 |     return decorator\n1367 | \n```\n"}, {"content": "Let me analyze the issue requirements and locate the relevant code areas:\n\n## Step 1: Let me summarize the key aspects of the feature request:\n\n1. The feature should:\n   - Allow converting old tags into new tags\n   - Allow converting new tags into old tags\n   - Provide warning for estimators implementing `_get_tags` or `_more_tags`\n   - Make `_safe_tags` raise a deprecation warning\n   - Enable `get_tags` to handle old tags conversion\n\n2. Main Components:\n   - `sklearn/utils/_tags.py`\n   - `sklearn/base.py`\n   - BaseEstimator class and its tag-related methods\n\n## Step 2: Let me identify the key functions and classes involved:\n\n1. From sklearn/utils/_tags.py:\n```python\ndef get_tags(estimator) -> Tags:\n    # Main function to get tags, needs to handle old tags conversion\n    pass\n\ndef _to_new_tags(old_tags) -> Tags:\n    # Converts old tags to new tags\n    pass\n\ndef _to_old_tags(new_tags) -> InputTags:\n    # Converts new tags to old tags\n    pass\n\ndef default_tags(estimator) -> Tags:\n    # Provides default tags when __sklearn_tags__ is not implemented\n    pass\n```\n\n2. From sklearn/base.py:\n```python\nclass BaseEstimator:\n    def __sklearn_tags__(self):\n        # Defines initial tags\n 